In chapter 2 I learned what reproducibility means in research and why it's important. The chapter discusses how reproducibility can be achieved in research projects through a set of tools that we will learn to use in this class. I learned in this chapter how "point and click" software can be a barrier to reproducibility in research and how code solves this problem by recording every step in the process. The chapter introduces each of the tools we will be using in this class and their purposes. I also learned in this chapter what the data in the dataset looks like, how it is recorded, and what it can tell us.
